{
  "name": "triathlon-wetsuit-reads-the-latest-measurement",
  "why": "`wetsuit_limit` at 24.5 °C: a wetsuit disqualifies when the latest water temperature in the entrant’s settled log is above the limit. Above it with a wetsuit is disqualified; above it without one, below it, and exactly on it (the comparison is strictly greater) are clean. Of two measurements the later decides, in both directions. And with no measurement taken the rule is false — a measurement nobody took is false, not a default — so a wetsuit nobody measured the water for is clean.",
